debian-config-system-hardening (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of debian-config-system-hardening package.
  * Add 50-system-hardening.conf for kernel self-protection parameters.
  * Add 50-disable-coredump.conf to prevent core dump memory leaks.
  * Enforce AppArmor dependency.
  * Enforce apt-listbugs dependency for listing critical bugs before each
    APT installation.
  * Enforce libpam-tmpdir dependency for per-user temporary directories.
  * Enforce libpam-pwquality dependency for password complexity enforcement.
  * Enforce needrestart for checking which daemons need to be restarted after
    library upgrades
  * Enforce needrestart-session for checking processes needed to be restarted
    in user sessions
  * Add 50-system-hardening.conf pwquality configuration drop-in under
    /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/.
  * Add password-quality PAM profile.
  * Add faillock-actions & faillock-preauth PAM profiles.
  * Update postinst script with POSIX set_config_key helper function to
    enforce password aging, UMASK 027, and hashing rounds in /etc/login.defs.
  * Expand sysctl baseline with dev.tty.ldisc_autoload,
    kernel.yama.ptrace_scope, kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled, and
    net.core.bpf_jit_harden.
  * Add 50-disable-coredump.sh profile drop-in under /etc/profile.d/ and
    50-disable-coredump.conf limits drop-in under /etc/security/limits.d/.
    (Closes: #100000)

 -- curtistinkers <curtistinkers@gmail.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:58:00 -0500
